Key insight
- The dominant remaining runtime loss is not DP dispatch itself; it is strict MAT/SWI paths that reach non-constructor scrutinee tags and then deopt via `aot_emit_ret_head` -> expression-mode `MAT` fallback (`EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG`).
- This confirms priority should move from DP-only forcing to a bounded strict-whnf strategy for non-constructor scrutinees (likely ALO/APP/SUP chain handling), with hard guards for correctness.

Operational notes
- Deterministic `--as-c` temp binary path (`hvm4-aot-as-c.main.bin`) still collides across concurrent runs; keep `--as-c` benchmark probes serial.
- Deopt report is opt-in; no stdout behavior change when `HVM_AOT_DEOPT` is unset.

Next likely step
- Add bounded strict scrutinee forcing beyond DP (`ALO`/`APP` first), but only by reusing existing runtime interaction helpers and fuel guards.
- Add a dedicated deopt reason for strict-match scrutinee-tag mismatch in head mode so this hotspot no longer hides behind generic `EXPR_UNSUPPORTED_TAG`.
